<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uyghurs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uyghur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uyghurs are a Turkic people who founded a powerful khaganate on the Mongolian steppe in the mid-eighth century after overthrowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-turkic-khaganate">Second Turkic Khaganate</a> in alliance with others. The Uyghur Khaganate became a major ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> before its collapse in 840. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> treat the Uyghurs as successors to Göktürk power in the steppe.</p></div>
